# CITATION.cff for AquaScan Open Science

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AquaScan Open Science: Multimodal Hydrogeophysical Groundwater Prospecting Research Framework"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "López Morales"
    given-names: "Ángel"
url: "https://github.com/angelopezvpb/aquascan-open-science"
repository-code: "https://github.com/angelopezvpb/aquascan-open-science"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-07"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - groundwater
  - hydrogeophysics
  - ert
  - seismic
  - open-science
  - machine-learning
  - geophysics
  - hydrology
abstract: >
  AquaScan Open Science is an open research framework for investigating
  multimodal hydrogeophysical approaches to groundwater prospecting.
  It integrates Electrical Resistivity Tomography (ERT), P-wave seismic,
  GNSS RTK positioning, and geological metadata with machine learning
  baselines for reproducible scientific experimentation. v0.2 adds a
  resumable, crash-safe national enrichment engine and an aggregate
  data-quality summary; the record-level dataset and model weights are
  not redistributed.
